@startuml VacApp-Backend-ClassDiagram
title VacApp — Diagrama de Clases del Backend (DDD/Hexagonal, 4 capas por Bounded Context)

top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 8
skinparam ranksep 18
hide empty members

legend top
  Cada Bounded Context se estructura en 4 capas. La dependencia apunta hacia adentro:
  **Interfaces (REST) -> Application -> Domain <- Infrastructure**.
  Los adaptadores de Infrastructure implementan ( ..|> ) los puertos (interfaces) del Domain/Application.
  Se omiten DTOs (Resources, Commands, Assemblers) por claridad.
endlegend

' #####################################################################
' COLUMNA IZQUIERDA
' #####################################################################

' ============================ IAM ============================
package "IAM" as BC_IAM #F4F8F2 {
  package "Interfaces" as IAM_I {
    class UserController
  }
  package "Application" as IAM_A {
    class UserCommandService
    class UserQueryService
  }
  package "Domain" as IAM_D {
    class User {
      +Id : int
      +Username : string
      +Email : string
      +Password : string
      +SubscriptionPlan : string
      +Role : UserRole
    }
    class PasswordResetToken {
      +UserId : int
      +CodeHash : string
      +ExpiresAt : DateTime
      +UsedAt : DateTime?
      +Attempts : int
      +MarkUsed()
    }
    enum UserRole {
      Rancher
      Admin
    }
    interface IUserRepository
    interface IPasswordResetTokenRepository
  }
  package "Infrastructure" as IAM_INF {
    class UserRepository
    class PasswordResetTokenRepository
    class HashingService <<BCrypt>>
    class TokenService <<JWT>>
  }
  IAM_I -[hidden]down- IAM_A
  IAM_A -[hidden]down- IAM_D
  IAM_D -[hidden]down- IAM_INF
}

